From: Orsavio P. Delmare <orsavio@delmare.lu>
Subject: [PATCH] ath11k: make the nss members unconditional so NSS=n builds

The NSS series does not compile with CPTCFG_ATH11K_NSS_SUPPORT off: core.h
puts the nss members of struct ath11k_vif and struct ath11k behind the ifdef,
while mac.c's AP_VLAN, WDS and dynamic-VLAN paths (patches 207/211/235/341)
dereference arvif->nss unguarded in about ten places, so the build dies with

  error: 'struct ath11k_vif' has no member named 'nss'   (x7)

Drop the guards rather than add ten #ifdefs. struct ath11k_peer already
carries its nss member unguarded, so this only makes the three consistent;
the types come from nss.h, which core.h includes unconditionally and which
defines them outside its own ifdef. Costs a few bytes per vif/pdev when NSS
is compiled out.

This has to be a late patch: editing 199-003 in place changes context that
later patches in the series rely on (notably the one adding bss_peer inside
the same ifdef), and they then fail to apply.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.h
@@ -458,9 +458,10 @@
 
 	struct ath11k_reg_tpc_power_info reg_tpc_info;
 	struct ath11k_mgmt_frame_stats mgmt_stats;
-#ifdef CPTCFG_ATH11K_NSS_SUPPORT
+	/* Deliberately not under CPTCFG_ATH11K_NSS_SUPPORT: mac.c's AP_VLAN,
+	 * WDS and dynamic-VLAN paths dereference arvif->nss unguarded.
+	 */
 	struct arvif_nss nss;
-#endif
 	struct list_head ap_vlan_arvifs;
 	/* list required by Dynamic VLAN during fw_recovery */
 	struct list_head dyn_vlan_cfg;
@@ -736,10 +737,8 @@
 	struct ath11k_pdev *pdev;
 	struct ieee80211_hw *hw;
 	struct ath11k_pdev_wmi *wmi;
-#ifdef CPTCFG_ATH11K_NSS_SUPPORT
 	struct ath11k_nss nss;
 	struct ath11k_peer *bss_peer;
-#endif
 	struct ath11k_pdev_dp dp;
 	u8 mac_addr[ETH_ALEN];
 	struct ath11k_he ar_he;
